  "description": {
    "sub_id3": null,
    "sub_name": "精微製造與淨零碳排",
    "sub_ename": "MICRO FABRICATION AND NET ZERO CARBON EMISSIONS",
    "describe_ch": "精微製造泛指各種機械加工及成形的微小化，包括微銑削、微放電、微研磨、微鍛造、微沖壓、微射出等技術，可應用於精密微形零件的製造。精微製造所用桌上型設備具有佔空間小、能量消耗少，本身即可對淨零碳排做出貢獻。此外，本課程也將介紹模具及成形製程之節能減碳作法。",
    "describe_eh": "Micro fabrication generally refers to the miniaturization of various mechanical machining and forming, including micro-milling, micro-EDM, micro-grinding, micro-forging, micro-stamping, micro-injection and other technologies, which can be applied to the manufacturing of precision micro parts. Desktop equipment used in micro fabrication takes up little space and consumes little energy, and can itself contribute to net-zero carbon emissions. In addition, this course will also introduce energy-saving and carbon-reducing practices for molds and forming processes.",
    "pre_subname": "",
    "pre_sub_id3": null,
    "pre_sub_ename": "",
    "pre_describe": null,
    "pre_describe_en": null,
    "scr_credit": 3.0
  },
